WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.620
Counter-deception is the defensive practice of reducing the harm caused by misleading

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.150
claims,

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.000
distorted context, manipulated evidence, and pressure-driven decisions.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.000
In this course, the word defensive matters.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The analyst is not trying to trick an adversary, embarrass a person, or win an argument.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.460
The analyst is trying to understand what is being claimed,

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.270
what decision depends on that claim, and what evidence is strong enough to support

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:21.760
action.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.490
Deception works best when people are rushed, emotionally loaded,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.310
or forced to decide with poor context.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.715
A suspicious message, a dramatic screenshot, a selective log excerpt,

00:00:29.715 --> 00:00:34.190
or a confident intelligence claim can all create momentum before anyone has verified

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.000
provenance.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Counter-deception slows that momentum down without freezing the organization.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.440
The operating question is simple: what do we know, how do we know it,

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.000
what remains uncertain, and what would change the decision?

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.265
This discipline applies across security operations, fraud review, insider risk,

00:00:48.265 --> 00:00:51.935
incident response, threat intelligence, and executive support.

00:00:51.935 --> 00:00:55.935
The same pattern appears in different forms: a claim arrives, a source is attached to it,

00:00:55.935 --> 00:00:58.190
evidence is offered or withheld, and someone is

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.935
pushed toward a decision.

00:00:59.935 --> 00:01:03.150
The analyst's job is to separate those pieces, preserve context, test alternatives,

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.380
and communicate confidence in a way decision makers can use.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.000
Ethical handling is not a side issue.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
A counter-deception review may involve people, accounts, devices, communications,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.845
telemetry, or sensitive artifacts.

00:01:13.845 --> 00:01:17.960
The work should protect privacy, maintain chain of custody, avoid amplifying harm,

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.000
and escalate through approved paths.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.210
Good counter-deception does not make analysts cynical.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:26.195
It makes them disciplined: curious, careful, transparent about uncertainty,

00:01:26.195 --> 00:01:28.000
and steady enough to verify before reacting.
